// Nepal Regions. Each map area is one of the 753 local levels (स्थानीय तह) of the Survey Department's boundaries of
// 2024: 6 metropolitan cities (महानगरपालिका), 11 sub-metropolitan cities (उपमहानगरपालिका), 276 municipalities (नगरपालिका)
// and 460 rural municipalities (गाउँपालिका), or one of the 22 pieces of national parks and reserves the file keeps
// apart (Chitwan, Bardiya, Shuklaphanta …: part of their district, not of a local level). Local levels are grouped into
// the 77 districts (जिल्ला) and these into the 7 provinces (प्रदेश). Each layer by its name in Latin letters or in Nepali.
// Latin names: provinces by the names their assemblies gave them (2018–2023: Koshi, Madhesh … Sudurpashchim); districts as the
// boundary file writes them, but Chitwan, Dhanusha, Kapilvastu and Tanahun (Chitawan, Dhanusa, Kapilbastu, Tanahu);
// local levels as the boundary file, with 15 slips mended against the Nepali name (Ilam, not Illam; Besishahar,
// Budhanilkantha, Parwanipur …) and 5 cities as their municipalities write themselves (Nepalgunj, Kapilvastu, Malangwa,
// Waling, Gaindakot: PALIKA_EN in tools/cache/builds/np-bt/scripts/nepal-common.mjs). Nepali names: the
// General Post Office's list of 2025 (the district and the local level without its type: पोखरा, not पोखरा महानगरपालिका),
// but where Wikipedia's lists and the Nepali Wikipedia agree on another spelling of a local level, theirs (106 of 753:
// काठमाडौँ, not काठमाण्डौ; इलाम, not ईलाम), and डडेलधुरा (GPO डँडेलधुरा). Local levels that share a name are asked with their district (Madi, Chitwan).
//
// Sources: Survey Department of Nepal, via OCHA COD-AB (cod-ab-npl v02, 2024, CC BY-IGO); General Post Office, Postal
// Code of Nepal (gpo.gov.np, 2025).

